      "units": [
        {
          "id": "s3-quick-01",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Amazon S three is object storage. You put data into buckets and retrieve it later, without managing storage servers. S three Standard is designed for eleven nines of durability. That’s about keeping your data safe from loss, not how often it’s reachable.",
          "text_sha256": "bdfa716bb4b9385d3783ee2e92dc09ab210c777d220e1279e7c0f54a364a3deb",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "582bd7af14f37161106114bd4131326c2db55ee1ed5f59d533ad0b80041a3324",
          "asset_sha256": "45344dfd91a610ef3d5ac881bc2e77949ea0d87c05fc9af4d9250f848a3c612b"
        },
        {
          "id": "s3-quick-02",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Use S three for things like customer uploads, backups, or logs you want to analyze later. A website, for example, can store photos in S three instead of on the web server.",
          "text_sha256": "5724aae8bde186e06492e45903a1499e40f68a6508e1f85a6059e9207c707ee8",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "c66ff33f9d5dcde3c2e118bdec481922f213a6aee79b76e5148b070e06655ad6",
          "asset_sha256": "45344dfd91a610ef3d5ac881bc2e77949ea0d87c05fc9af4d9250f848a3c612b"
        },
        {
          "id": "s3-quick-03",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Say the site uploads a cat photo. The photo and its metadata make up the object. The bucket is the container, and images slash cat dot jay peg is the full key you use to retrieve that photo.",
          "text_sha256": "7559ed82dc0d872923b90f2f1a119551e540041dee569b3e5a5a790144936fbb",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "893191bc77a4d48d191f184f9bb61c07190c7cc4c9f13d2a1e317c88d528d1c7",
          "asset_sha256": "45344dfd91a610ef3d5ac881bc2e77949ea0d87c05fc9af4d9250f848a3c612b"
        },
        {
          "id": "s3-quick-04",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "Choose a storage class by access pattern. Standard suits frequent reads. Intelligent Tiering handles changing access. Glacier classes are built for archives. Some need a restore before you can read the data.",
          "text_sha256": "4b0bb6126566a3739091e4e0fbd0105376a97d33849ff4a7eea0a045e76db46f",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "cc9cda1207cbc5ca469d29faf025d4c48686cbc5c4f5e02010a6ad7c94adf6e2",
          "asset_sha256": "45344dfd91a610ef3d5ac881bc2e77949ea0d87c05fc9af4d9250f848a3c612b"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
